Here the branch condition changed from `body` (trimmed body truthiness) to `_adoThreadRawBody(rootComment)` (RAW body truthiness). The PR says: "whitespace-only ADO comment rendering its author line" is a quirk pinned, not fixed. For a whitespace-only body: raw = '  ' (truthy), trimmed = '' (falsy). Original: else-branch → `_[No comment body]_\n`. New: if-branch → `**author** (date):\n` (body = trimmed = empty string). That IS a behavior change for whitespace-only comments!

Wait, unless the original also used raw truthiness... Original: `if (body)` where `var body = (rootComment && rootComment.content) || '';` — raw body. Then renders `body.trim()`. So ORIGINAL used RAW truthiness! `if (body)` — body is raw ('  ' is truthy) → renders author line with empty trimmed body. New: `_adoThreadRawBody(rootComment)` truthy → same. So the new code PRESERVES the original raw-truthiness quirk. 

The PR description says "whitespace-only ADO comment rendering its author line" — pinned, not fixed. Correct, that's preserved.

Now the `_gitlabRenderThreadSection` — in GitLab original, `section += body ? ...` where `var body = (root.body || '').trim();` — TRIMMED truthiness. New: `mapped.body ? ...` where mapped.body is trimmed. Same trimmed truthiness. OK so branch selection is the same.

